      "title": "Ground | FORGE Methodology | Embracing Digital",
      "summary": "Ground | FORGE Methodology | Embracing Digital Embracing Digital Home Guidance Briefings (EDTW) What changed Interviews (EDT) How others did it Architectural Deep Dives What to do next Learn Digital Transformation Overview Pillars AI, Cyber, Data, Edge, Computing, Comms ODXA Domains &amp; mappings Whitepapers Monthly synthesis Articles Explainers &amp; analysis Lectures (DTA) Learning series Community Community Newsletter Patreon LinkedIn About About Host Sponsors Shop Search Ground Root in Reality Stabilize and Capitalize The Ground stage is the stabilization and foundation-building phase of the FORGE methodology within the GEAR framework. Rather than pursuing high-risk rip-and-replace strategies, it anchors new digital capabilities in proven enterprise strengths, existing data stores, and operational infrastructure across the transformation dimensions. Establishing robust governance, secure baseline integrations, and resilient platforms ensures that subsequent transformations build on stable, sustainable architectural foundations. Leverage Strengths Identify what is already working well. Capitalize on existing high-performing teams, reliable systems, and efficient processes within the O-DXA domains. Infrastructure Anchoring Root new digital capabilities in current physical and digital reality. Ensure that transformation doesn't drift into abstract theory but remains technically feasible. Avoid \"Rip and Replace\" Favor evolutionary change over destructive replacement. By grounding transformation in the present, we reduce risk and maintain mission continuity. Key Activities Current Asset Optimization: Identify ways to improve or extend the life of existing systems. Constraint Integration: Build the transformation plan around the non-negotiable physical and digital constraints of the terrain. Pilot Implementation: Test reconciled designs in a controlled, real-world environment to ensure they are properly grounded. Culture Anchoring: Ensure that new processes and techn",
