      "title": "The FORGE Methodology | Applied Practice | Embracing Digital",
      "summary": "The FORGE Methodology | Applied Practice | Embracing Digital Embracing Digital Home Guidance Briefings (EDTW) What changed Interviews (EDT) How others did it Architectural Deep Dives What to do next Learn Digital Transformation Overview Pillars AI, Cyber, Data, Edge, Computing, Comms ODXA Domains &amp; mappings Whitepapers Monthly synthesis Articles Explainers &amp; analysis Lectures (DTA) Learning series Community Community Newsletter Patreon LinkedIn About About Host Sponsors Shop Search Architectural FORGE The Applied Practice of the GEAR System Architecture as Execution Architectural FORGE is the active delivery methodology and execution engine within the GEAR framework. It provides a structured, iterative five-stage practice—Find, Observe, Reconcile, Ground, and Enhance—that translates high-level enterprise architecture and strategy into operational reality. By systematically discovering existing assets, analyzing workflows, resolving misalignment, and scaling validated capabilities, FORGE eliminates the high failure rates of traditional digital transformations. Mission outcomes delivered through integrated digital capabilities Mission Solutions &amp; Capabilities Architectural FORGE: The active process that connects and aligns all transformation pillars Architectural FORGE Find Find: Identify gaps, silos, and opportunities across domains • Observe Observe: Gather data and validate current state reality • Reconcile Reconcile: Align strategic intent with operational execution • Ground Ground: Root transformation in physical and digital reality • Enhance Enhance: Scale and optimize capabilities for the future Cloud, DevOps, emerging compute, and decentralized platforms enabling portable execution everywhere Ubiquitous Computing Edge Computing enables data processing and decision-making closer to where data is generated to support low-latency, resilient, and mission-critical operations. Edge Computing Artificial Intelligence enables systems to learn, reason, and a",
