      "id": 378,
      "title": "Observe | FORGE Methodology | Embracing Digital",
      "summary": "Observe | FORGE Methodology | Embracing Digital Embracing Digital Home Guidance Briefings (EDTW) What changed Interviews (EDT) How others did it Architectural Deep Dives What to do next Learn Digital Transformation Overview Pillars AI, Cyber, Data, Edge, Computing, Comms ODXA Domains &amp; mappings Whitepapers Monthly synthesis Articles Explainers &amp; analysis Lectures (DTA) Learning series Community Community Newsletter Patreon LinkedIn About About Host Sponsors Shop Search Observe Understand Usage Analyze the Interactions The Observe stage is the behavioral analysis phase of the FORGE methodology within the GEAR framework. Moving beyond static inventories, it examines the dynamic interactions, data flows, user behaviors, and operational friction occurring across the enterprise in real time. Analyzing how systems and personnel actually function under operational conditions provides architects with the empirical evidence needed to diagnose root inefficiencies and validate architectural assumptions. Data Flow Mapping Trace how information moves between domains. Identify the bottlenecks, circular dependencies, and manual \"bridge\" steps that slow down operations. The Nervous System Understand the interdependencies between systems. If one component fails, what else is affected? Map the ripple effects across the enterprise. Actual vs. Intended Usage Compare how a system was designed to be used with how it is actually being used. Discrepancies here often signal friction or missing capabilities. Key Activities Runtime Analysis: Use logs, telemetry, and monitoring tools to observe systems in action. Process Observability: Shadow employees as they perform tasks to see the \"real-world\" process flow. Dependency Mapping: Build a graph of how components rely on one another across O-DXA domains. Measurement: Establish baseline metrics for performance, reliability, and user satisfaction. Previous: Find Next: Reconcile Next Steps on Your Transformation Journey Use the Six Pillars",
